  "id": "DrugBank_DB00833 - MONDO_24313",
  "verbalization": "Cefaclor, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is implicated in the treatment of Staphylococcal Infection through a chain of indications that link it to Staphylococcus Aureus Infection. The evidence suggests that Cefaclor is used to treat Staphylococcus Aureus Infection, which in turn is associated with Staphylococcal Infection. This implies that Cefaclor may have a role in the treatment of staphylococcal infections by targeting the bacteria that cause them. The indirect pathway through Dirithromycin and Dicloxacillin, which are also used in the treatment of staphylococcal infections, further supports the notion that Cefaclor could be part of a broader therapeutic strategy for these infections. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Cefaclor to be repurposed for the treatment of staphylococcal infections, particularly in cases where other antibiotics may not be effective.",
